# Proposed features recognized from step_hole.step by sidecar/import_step.py
# (contract v1 -- see sidecar/CONTRACT.md). Review before use:
# recognition proposes, it does not machine.

# F3: planar, normal +Z, topmost planar face (CHECKLIST row 1.1)
feature F3_Top Plane(z=10.0)

# F8: outer profile under top cap F3: vertical wall loop F4 F1 F2 F8 F10 F9, top at z=10.0, base at z=6.0, material inside the loop; stepped base: the profile stops at the highest base z=6.0, and F1 to z=0.0, F2 to z=0.0, F4 to z=0.0, F10 to z=0.0 run on below it (CHECKLIST row 2.8)
# consume with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F8_Profile, comp=control)  [the feature carries its own z + extent]
# the loop is wound CW: material inside, tool outside (the winding convention,
# DECISIONS.md -> "Row-2.4 side selector")
# comp=control is required on Contour runs: recognized boundaries carry rounded
# corners tessellated to chords, and engine comp hard-errors on rounded-corner
# offsets (DECISIONS.md -> "recognized contours propose comp=control")
# the base is stepped: this profile stops at z=6.0, the highest base; the walls F1 F2 F4 F10 run on below it
# and belong to whatever stands lower -- declare that by hand or accept its own proposal
feature F8_Profile ProfileBoss(z=10.0, extent=4.0
    0.0 0.0
    0.0 40.0
    30.0 40.0
    30.0 16.0
    29.455 15.963
    28.921 15.852
    28.406 15.669
    27.922 15.418
    27.476 15.103
    27.077 14.73
    26.732 14.307
    26.448 13.84
    26.231 13.34
    26.084 12.814
    26.009 12.273
    26.009 11.727
    26.084 11.186
    26.231 10.66
    26.448 10.16
    26.732 9.693
    27.077 9.27
    27.476 8.897
    27.922 8.582
    28.406 8.331
    28.921 8.148
    29.455 8.037
    30.0 8.0
    30.0 0.0
)

# F10: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; bottom opens through -- a drillable through hole (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# consume with: run Form(points=[F10_Hole], tool=..., cycle=Simple)  [the bore carries its own extent, measured down from the stock top]
# through hole -- drill past extent=10.0 by the tip's point length for full-diameter breakthrough
# or finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F10_Hole, stepover=...)
feature F10_Hole CylinderBore(dia=8.0, extent=10.0, x=30.0, y=12.0)

# F11: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; flat floor F13 -- a milled bore, with a smaller hole on the same axis opening in the floor (a counterbore) (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F11_Bore, stepover=...)  [stepover is the ring spacing up the wall]
# a flat floor is milled, not drilled -- a twist drill leaves a conical point, so no drill run is suggested
feature F11_Bore CylinderBore(dia=12.0, extent=4.0, x=15.0, y=28.0)

# F12: cylindrical, axis +Z, full revolution, material outside (a bore), opens upward; bottom opens through -- a drillable through hole; rim at z=6.0, 4.0 below the stock top z=10.0, with open air straight above it to the top -- proposed from the top, where a drill through the blank starts, extent 10.0 the whole way down; what the model has above the rim is another feature's to cut (CHECKLIST row 2.3)
# consume with: run Form(points=[F12_Hole], tool=..., cycle=Simple)  [the bore carries its own extent, measured down from the stock top]
# through hole -- drill past extent=10.0 by the tip's point length for full-diameter breakthrough
# or finish the wall with: run Side(tool=..., surface=F12_Hole, stepover=...)
feature F12_Hole CylinderBore(dia=6.0, extent=10.0, x=15.0, y=28.0)
